NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useHotkeyRecorder"},{"type":"text","value":" to build a shortcut customization UI. Recording defaults to physical codes, producing values such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Mod+[KeyS]"},{"type":"text","value":". Store that value directly and pass it to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useHotkey"},{"type":"text","value":". Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"formatForDisplay"},{"type":"text","value":" for the label."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Hotkeys automatically suppresses registered hotkey and sequence callbacks while any recorder is active. You do not need to set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enabled"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isRecording"},{"type":"text","value":". Registrations remain available for conflict detection, and recorded keys stay suppressed through repeats and key release."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"basic-usage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic usage"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useState } from 'octane'\nimport { useHotkey, useHotkeyRecorder, formatForDisplay } from '@tanstack/octane-hotkeys'\nimport type { Hotkey } from '@tanstack/octane-hotkeys'\n\nexport function ShortcutSettings() @{\n\tconst [binding, setBinding] = useState<Hotkey>('Mod+S')\n\tconst recorder = useHotkeyRecorder({\n\t\tonRecord: setBinding,\n\t\tonClear: () => setBinding('Mod+S'),\n\t})\n\tuseHotkey(binding, () => console.log('Saved'))\n\n\t<div>\n\t\t<kbd>{formatForDisplay(binding)}</kbd>\n\t\t<button type=\"button\" onClick={recorder.startRecording}>Record</button>\n\t\t@if (recorder.isRecording) {\n\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t<p>Press a shortcut. Escape cancels; Backspace resets the binding.</p>\n\t\t\t\t<button type=\"button\" onClick={recorder.cancelRecording}>Cancel</button>\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t}\n\t</div>\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This example stores the replacement binding in application state and restores "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Mod+S"},{"type":"text","value":" when the user clears it. Cancellation leaves the saved binding unchanged."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"return-value","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return value"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Property"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Meaning"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isRecording"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Whether a session is active."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recordedHotkey"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Hotkey | null"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The recorded binding, or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" after starting, stopping, or cancelling."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"startRecording"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"() => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Start a new session."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stopRecording"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"() => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stop and clear recorder state without calling "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onRecord"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onCancel"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cancelRecording"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"() => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stop, clear recorder state, and call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onCancel"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read the returned state on each component render."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"recordby","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recordBy"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The default is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'code'"},{"type":"text","value":". On macOS, Option+S producing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ß"},{"type":"text","value":" records "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Alt+[KeyS]"},{"type":"text","value":", and Option+2 producing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"™"},{"type":"text","value":" records "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Alt+[Digit2]"},{"type":"text","value":". Stored brackets preserve physical identity through serialization and registration. Existing authored strings such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Mod+S"},{"type":"text","value":" remain logical."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recordBy: 'key'"},{"type":"text","value":" to record the produced character. Code mode rejects an event without a usable code and never falls back to key mode. IME composition is ignored. AltGraph character entry is rejected in code mode; key mode preserves the character without synthetic Control/Alt while retaining Shift."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"onrecord","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onRecord"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Receives the recorded "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Hotkey"},{"type":"text","value":" when the user enters a valid chord. A chord can be a single non-modifier key or a key with modifiers. Update your saved binding here."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"oncancel","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onCancel"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Runs when Escape cancels a session or when you call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cancelRecording()"},{"type":"text","value":". Use it to exit an editing state without changing the saved binding."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"onclear","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onClear"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Runs when the user presses unmodified Backspace or Delete during recording. Clearing calls only "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onClear"},{"type":"text","value":"; it does not call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onRecord"},{"type":"text","value":". Your application decides whether to remove the binding or restore an initial value."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"shared-defaults-and-changing-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Shared defaults and changing options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hotkeyRecorder"},{"type":"text","value":" defaults in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HotkeysProvider"},{"type":"text","value":". Options passed to an individual hook override provider defaults. For a plural hook, each definition's options override its common options. See the "},{"type":"link","href":"../quick-start.md#default-options-provider","children":[{"type":"text","value":"provider setup"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options and callbacks refresh after every commit, so callbacks see current component state."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"recording-behavior","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recording behavior"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Input"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Behavior"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Modifier alone"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wait for a non-modifier key."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Modifier plus a non-modifier key"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Record the chord and finish."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Single non-modifier key, such as F1"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Record the key and finish."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Escape"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cancel."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Unmodified Backspace or Delete"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Clear and call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onClear"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Automatic key repeat or IME composition"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Do not record a new chord."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recording events, repeats, and their key releases do not trigger registered hotkeys or sequences."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"ignoreinputs","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ignoreInputs"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":". Normal typing in inputs, textareas, selects, and contentEditable elements passes through. Escape still cancels while an input is focused. Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ignoreInputs: false"},{"type":"text","value":" to capture shortcuts from a focused input."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"mod-auto-conversion","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mod auto-conversion"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On macOS, Command+S becomes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Mod+[KeyS]"},{"type":"text","value":". Reusing that binding on Windows resolves "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Mod"},{"type":"text","value":" to Control while preserving the physical key position. Pass a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"platform"},{"type":"text","value":" option when detection must be overridden."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"validation-and-conflicts","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Validation and conflicts"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Supply these options alongside "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onRecord"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import type { HotkeyRecorderOptions } from '@tanstack/octane-hotkeys'\n\nconst options: HotkeyRecorderOptions = {\n\tonRecord: (hotkey) => console.log('Accepted', hotkey),\n\tdetectConflicts: {\n\t\t// Replace this with the ID from the live registration being edited.\n\t\texcludeIds: ['registration-being-edited'],\n\t\ttarget: document,\n\t\teventType: 'keydown',\n\t},\n\tvalidate: (_hotkey, { parsedHotkey }) =>\n\t\tparsedHotkey.modifiers.length > 0 || 'Include a modifier.',\n\tonReject: ({ reason, message, conflicts }) => {\n\t\tconsole.log(reason, message, conflicts)\n\t},\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"validate"},{"type":"text","value":" returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" to accept, or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":" or a message to reject. Validation runs before commit. A rejected candidate leaves recording active. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onReject"},{"type":"text","value":" reports "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"missing-code"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"alt-graph"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"invalid"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"validation"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"conflict"},{"type":"text","value":", plus the candidate when available and conflicting views for a conflict."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"detectConflicts: true"},{"type":"text","value":" checks enabled live registrations with the intended event type, defaulting to keydown, and overlapping targets, defaulting to document. Document and nested element scopes can conflict; disjoint widgets can reuse a binding. The options object supports "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scope: 'all'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"includeDisabled"},{"type":"text","value":", and an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"exclude(registration)"},{"type":"text","value":" predicate."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Checks include single bindings and sequence prefixes. Source events detect physical/logical overlap on the recorded layout. This is conservative collision detection: propagation, input filtering, match priority, external listeners, unmounted routes, and other layouts can change dispatch."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For checks outside recording, call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"findHotkeyConflicts(bindingOrSequence, options)"},{"type":"text","value":". Without source "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"events"},{"type":"text","value":", it compares identities and prefixes rather than guessing which logical character a physical position produces."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"building-a-shortcut-settings-ui","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Building a shortcut settings UI"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For several actions, keep the bindings in an array or object and record the ID of the action being edited. On "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onRecord"},{"type":"text","value":", replace that action's binding and clear the editing ID. On "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onCancel"},{"type":"text","value":", clear only the editing ID. Use the plural registration API for the current list."}]},{"type":"code","value":"useHotkeys(shortcuts.map((shortcut) => ({\n\thotkey: shortcut.hotkey,\n\tcallback: () => runAction(shortcut.id),\n\toptions: { meta: { name: shortcut.name } },\n})))","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"link","href":"../examples/useHotkeyRecorder","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useHotkeyRecorder example"}]},{"type":"text","value":" includes multiple actions, editable names and descriptions, create/delete controls, reset and clear behavior, cancellation, and a live registry. The "},{"type":"link","href":"../examples/kitchen-sink","children":[{"type":"text","value":"kitchen sink"}]},{"type":"text","value":" also demonstrates conflict feedback and physical versus logical recording."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"under-the-hood","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Under the hood"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Octane uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/octane-store"},{"type":"text","value":" to subscribe to the recorder. The hook destroys its recorder on unmount. The core "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HotkeyRecorder"},{"type":"text","value":" owns the recording listeners. Store the accepted binding in application state rather than relying on recorder session state as your preferences store."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"basic-usage","text":"Basic usage","level":2},{"id":"return-value","text":"Return value","level":2},{"id":"options","text":"Options","level":2},{"id":"recordby","text":"recordBy","level":3},{"id":"onrecord","text":"onRecord","level":3},{"id":"oncancel","text":"onCancel","level":3},{"id":"onclear","text":"onClear","level":3},{"id":"shared-defaults-and-changing-options","text":"Shared defaults and changing options","level":3},{"id":"recording-behavior","text":"Recording behavior","level":2},{"id":"ignoreinputs","text":"ignoreInputs","level":3},{"id":"mod-auto-conversion","text":"Mod auto-conversion","level":3},{"id":"validation-and-conflicts","text":"Validation and conflicts","level":2},{"id":"building-a-shortcut-settings-ui","text":"Building a shortcut settings UI","level":2},{"id":"under-the-hood","text":"Under the hood","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nUse `useHotkeyRecorder` to build a shortcut customization UI. Recording defaults to physical codes, producing values such as `Mod+[KeyS]`. Store that value directly and pass it to `useHotkey`. Use `formatForDisplay` for the label.\n\nTanStack Hotkeys automatically suppresses registered hotkey and sequence callbacks while any recorder is active. You do not need to set `enabled` from `isRecording`. Registrations remain available for conflict detection, and recorded keys stay suppressed through repeats and key release.\n\n## Basic usage\n\n\n```tsx\nimport { useState } from 'octane'\nimport { useHotkey, useHotkeyRecorder, formatForDisplay } from '@tanstack/octane-hotkeys'\nimport type { Hotkey } from '@tanstack/octane-hotkeys'\n\nexport function ShortcutSettings() @{\n\tconst [binding, setBinding] = useState<Hotkey>('Mod+S')\n\tconst recorder = useHotkeyRecorder({\n\t\tonRecord: setBinding,\n\t\tonClear: () => setBinding('Mod+S'),\n\t})\n\tuseHotkey(binding, () => console.log('Saved'))\n\n\t<div>\n\t\t<kbd>{formatForDisplay(binding)}</kbd>\n\t\t<button type=\"button\" onClick={recorder.startRecording}>Record</button>\n\t\t@if (recorder.isRecording) {\n\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t<p>Press a shortcut. Escape cancels; Backspace resets the binding.</p>\n\t\t\t\t<button type=\"button\" onClick={recorder.cancelRecording}>Cancel</button>\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t}\n\t</div>\n}\n```\n\nThis example stores the replacement binding in application state and restores `Mod+S` when the user clears it. Cancellation leaves the saved binding unchanged.\n\n## Return value\n\n| Property | Type | Meaning |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `isRecording` | `boolean` | Whether a session is active. |\n| `recordedHotkey` | `Hotkey \\| null` | The recorded binding, or `null` after starting, stopping, or cancelling. |\n| `startRecording` | `() => void` | Start a new session. |\n| `stopRecording` | `() => void` | Stop and clear recorder state without calling `onRecord` or `onCancel`. |\n| `cancelRecording` | `() => void` | Stop, clear recorder state, and call `onCancel`. |\n\nRead the returned state on each component render.\n\n## Options\n\n### `recordBy`\n\nThe default is `'code'`. On macOS, Option+S producing `ß` records `Alt+[KeyS]`, and Option+2 producing `™` records `Alt+[Digit2]`. Stored brackets preserve physical identity through serialization and registration. Existing authored strings such as `Mod+S` remain logical.\n\nSet `recordBy: 'key'` to record the produced character. Code mode rejects an event without a usable code and never falls back to key mode. IME composition is ignored. AltGraph character entry is rejected in code mode; key mode preserves the character without synthetic Control/Alt while retaining Shift.\n\n### `onRecord`\n\nReceives the recorded `Hotkey` when the user enters a valid chord. A chord can be a single non-modifier key or a key with modifiers. Update your saved binding here.\n\n### `onCancel`\n\nRuns when Escape cancels a session or when you call `cancelRecording()`. Use it to exit an editing state without changing the saved binding.\n\n### `onClear`\n\nRuns when the user presses unmodified Backspace or Delete during recording. Clearing calls only `onClear`; it does not call `onRecord`. Your application decides whether to remove the binding or restore an initial value.\n\n### Shared defaults and changing options\n\nSet `hotkeyRecorder` defaults in `HotkeysProvider`. Options passed to an individual hook override provider defaults. For a plural hook, each definition's options override its common options. See the [provider setup](../quick-start.md#default-options-provider).\n\nOptions and callbacks refresh after every commit, so callbacks see current component state.\n\n## Recording behavior\n\n| Input | Behavior |\n| --- | --- |\n| Modifier alone | Wait for a non-modifier key. |\n| Modifier plus a non-modifier key | Record the chord and finish. |\n| Single non-modifier key, such as F1 | Record the key and finish. |\n| Escape | Cancel. |\n| Unmodified Backspace or Delete | Clear and call `onClear`. |\n| Automatic key repeat or IME composition | Do not record a new chord. |\n\nRecording events, repeats, and their key releases do not trigger registered hotkeys or sequences.\n\n### `ignoreInputs`\n\nThis defaults to `true`. Normal typing in inputs, textareas, selects, and contentEditable elements passes through. Escape still cancels while an input is focused. Set `ignoreInputs: false` to capture shortcuts from a focused input.\n\n### Mod auto-conversion\n\nOn macOS, Command+S becomes `Mod+[KeyS]`. Reusing that binding on Windows resolves `Mod` to Control while preserving the physical key position. Pass a `platform` option when detection must be overridden.\n\n## Validation and conflicts\n\nSupply these options alongside `onRecord`:\n\n```ts\nimport type { HotkeyRecorderOptions } from '@tanstack/octane-hotkeys'\n\nconst options: HotkeyRecorderOptions = {\n\tonRecord: (hotkey) => console.log('Accepted', hotkey),\n\tdetectConflicts: {\n\t\t// Replace this with the ID from the live registration being edited.\n\t\texcludeIds: ['registration-being-edited'],\n\t\ttarget: document,\n\t\teventType: 'keydown',\n\t},\n\tvalidate: (_hotkey, { parsedHotkey }) =>\n\t\tparsedHotkey.modifiers.length > 0 || 'Include a modifier.',\n\tonReject: ({ reason, message, conflicts }) => {\n\t\tconsole.log(reason, message, conflicts)\n\t},\n}\n```\n\n`validate` returns `true` to accept, or `false` or a message to reject. Validation runs before commit. A rejected candidate leaves recording active. `onReject` reports `missing-code`, `alt-graph`, `invalid`, `validation`, or `conflict`, plus the candidate when available and conflicting views for a conflict.\n\n`detectConflicts: true` checks enabled live registrations with the intended event type, defaulting to keydown, and overlapping targets, defaulting to document. Document and nested element scopes can conflict; disjoint widgets can reuse a binding. The options object supports `scope: 'all'`, `includeDisabled`, and an `exclude(registration)` predicate.\n\nChecks include single bindings and sequence prefixes. Source events detect physical/logical overlap on the recorded layout. This is conservative collision detection: propagation, input filtering, match priority, external listeners, unmounted routes, and other layouts can change dispatch.\n\nFor checks outside recording, call `findHotkeyConflicts(bindingOrSequence, options)`. Without source `events`, it compares identities and prefixes rather than guessing which logical character a physical position produces.\n\n## Building a shortcut settings UI\n\nFor several actions, keep the bindings in an array or object and record the ID of the action being edited. On `onRecord`, replace that action's binding and clear the editing ID. On `onCancel`, clear only the editing ID. Use the plural registration API for the current list.\n\n```tsx\nuseHotkeys(shortcuts.map((shortcut) => ({\n\thotkey: shortcut.hotkey,\n\tcallback: () => runAction(shortcut.id),\n\toptions: { meta: { name: shortcut.name } },\n})))\n```\n\nThe [useHotkeyRecorder example](../examples/useHotkeyRecorder) includes multiple actions, editable names and descriptions, create/delete controls, reset and clear behavior, cancellation, and a live registry. The [kitchen sink](../examples/kitchen-sink) also demonstrates conflict feedback and physical versus logical recording.\n\n## Under the hood\n\nOctane uses `@tanstack/octane-store` to subscribe to the recorder. The hook destroys its recorder on unmount. The core `HotkeyRecorder` owns the recording listeners. Store the accepted binding in application state rather than relying on recorder session state as your preferences store.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Hotkey Recording Guide\nid: hotkey-recording\n---\n\nUse `useHotkeyRecorder` to build a shortcut customization UI. Recording defaults to physical codes, producing values such as `Mod+[KeyS]`. Store that value directly and pass it to `useHotkey`. Use `formatForDisplay` for the label.\n\nTanStack Hotkeys automatically suppresses registered hotkey and sequence callbacks while any recorder is active. You do not need to set `enabled` from `isRecording`. Registrations remain available for conflict detection, and recorded keys stay suppressed through repeats and key release.\n\n## Basic usage\n\n\n```tsx\nimport { useState } from 'octane'\nimport { useHotkey, useHotkeyRecorder, formatForDisplay } from '@tanstack/octane-hotkeys'\nimport type { Hotkey } from '@tanstack/octane-hotkeys'\n\nexport function ShortcutSettings() @{\n\tconst [binding, setBinding] = useState<Hotkey>('Mod+S')\n\tconst recorder = useHotkeyRecorder({\n\t\tonRecord: setBinding,\n\t\tonClear: () => setBinding('Mod+S'),\n\t})\n\tuseHotkey(binding, () => console.log('Saved'))\n\n\t<div>\n\t\t<kbd>{formatForDisplay(binding)}</kbd>\n\t\t<button type=\"button\" onClick={recorder.startRecording}>Record</button>\n\t\t@if (recorder.isRecording) {\n\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t<p>Press a shortcut. Escape cancels; Backspace resets the binding.</p>\n\t\t\t\t<button type=\"button\" onClick={recorder.cancelRecording}>Cancel</button>\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t}\n\t</div>\n}\n```\n\nThis example stores the replacement binding in application state and restores `Mod+S` when the user clears it. Cancellation leaves the saved binding unchanged.\n\n## Return value\n\n| Property | Type | Meaning |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `isRecording` | `boolean` | Whether a session is active. |\n| `recordedHotkey` | `Hotkey \\| null` | The recorded binding, or `null` after starting, stopping, or cancelling. |\n| `startRecording` | `() => void` | Start a new session. |\n| `stopRecording` | `() => void` | Stop and clear recorder state without calling `onRecord` or `onCancel`. |\n| `cancelRecording` | `() => void` | Stop, clear recorder state, and call `onCancel`. |\n\nRead the returned state on each component render.\n\n## Options\n\n### `recordBy`\n\nThe default is `'code'`. On macOS, Option+S producing `ß` records `Alt+[KeyS]`, and Option+2 producing `™` records `Alt+[Digit2]`. Stored brackets preserve physical identity through serialization and registration. Existing authored strings such as `Mod+S` remain logical.\n\nSet `recordBy: 'key'` to record the produced character. Code mode rejects an event without a usable code and never falls back to key mode. IME composition is ignored. AltGraph character entry is rejected in code mode; key mode preserves the character without synthetic Control/Alt while retaining Shift.\n\n### `onRecord`\n\nReceives the recorded `Hotkey` when the user enters a valid chord. A chord can be a single non-modifier key or a key with modifiers. Update your saved binding here.\n\n### `onCancel`\n\nRuns when Escape cancels a session or when you call `cancelRecording()`. Use it to exit an editing state without changing the saved binding.\n\n### `onClear`\n\nRuns when the user presses unmodified Backspace or Delete during recording. Clearing calls only `onClear`; it does not call `onRecord`. Your application decides whether to remove the binding or restore an initial value.\n\n### Shared defaults and changing options\n\nSet `hotkeyRecorder` defaults in `HotkeysProvider`. Options passed to an individual hook override provider defaults. For a plural hook, each definition's options override its common options. See the [provider setup](../quick-start.md#default-options-provider).\n\nOptions and callbacks refresh after every commit, so callbacks see current component state.\n\n## Recording behavior\n\n| Input | Behavior |\n| --- | --- |\n| Modifier alone | Wait for a non-modifier key. |\n| Modifier plus a non-modifier key | Record the chord and finish. |\n| Single non-modifier key, such as F1 | Record the key and finish. |\n| Escape | Cancel. |\n| Unmodified Backspace or Delete | Clear and call `onClear`. |\n| Automatic key repeat or IME composition | Do not record a new chord. |\n\nRecording events, repeats, and their key releases do not trigger registered hotkeys or sequences.\n\n### `ignoreInputs`\n\nThis defaults to `true`. Normal typing in inputs, textareas, selects, and contentEditable elements passes through. Escape still cancels while an input is focused. Set `ignoreInputs: false` to capture shortcuts from a focused input.\n\n### Mod auto-conversion\n\nOn macOS, Command+S becomes `Mod+[KeyS]`. Reusing that binding on Windows resolves `Mod` to Control while preserving the physical key position. Pass a `platform` option when detection must be overridden.\n\n## Validation and conflicts\n\nSupply these options alongside `onRecord`:\n\n```ts\nimport type { HotkeyRecorderOptions } from '@tanstack/octane-hotkeys'\n\nconst options: HotkeyRecorderOptions = {\n\tonRecord: (hotkey) => console.log('Accepted', hotkey),\n\tdetectConflicts: {\n\t\t// Replace this with the ID from the live registration being edited.\n\t\texcludeIds: ['registration-being-edited'],\n\t\ttarget: document,\n\t\teventType: 'keydown',\n\t},\n\tvalidate: (_hotkey, { parsedHotkey }) =>\n\t\tparsedHotkey.modifiers.length > 0 || 'Include a modifier.',\n\tonReject: ({ reason, message, conflicts }) => {\n\t\tconsole.log(reason, message, conflicts)\n\t},\n}\n```\n\n`validate` returns `true` to accept, or `false` or a message to reject. Validation runs before commit. A rejected candidate leaves recording active. `onReject` reports `missing-code`, `alt-graph`, `invalid`, `validation`, or `conflict`, plus the candidate when available and conflicting views for a conflict.\n\n`detectConflicts: true` checks enabled live registrations with the intended event type, defaulting to keydown, and overlapping targets, defaulting to document. Document and nested element scopes can conflict; disjoint widgets can reuse a binding. The options object supports `scope: 'all'`, `includeDisabled`, and an `exclude(registration)` predicate.\n\nChecks include single bindings and sequence prefixes. Source events detect physical/logical overlap on the recorded layout. This is conservative collision detection: propagation, input filtering, match priority, external listeners, unmounted routes, and other layouts can change dispatch.\n\nFor checks outside recording, call `findHotkeyConflicts(bindingOrSequence, options)`. Without source `events`, it compares identities and prefixes rather than guessing which logical character a physical position produces.\n\n## Building a shortcut settings UI\n\nFor several actions, keep the bindings in an array or object and record the ID of the action being edited. On `onRecord`, replace that action's binding and clear the editing ID. On `onCancel`, clear only the editing ID. Use the plural registration API for the current list.\n\n```tsx\nuseHotkeys(shortcuts.map((shortcut) => ({\n\thotkey: shortcut.hotkey,\n\tcallback: () => runAction(shortcut.id),\n\toptions: { meta: { name: shortcut.name } },\n})))\n```\n\nThe [useHotkeyRecorder example](../examples/useHotkeyRecorder) includes multiple actions, editable names and descriptions, create/delete controls, reset and clear behavior, cancellation, and a live registry. The [kitchen sink](../examples/kitchen-sink) also demonstrates conflict feedback and physical versus logical recording.\n\n## Under the hood\n\nOctane uses `@tanstack/octane-store` to subscribe to the recorder. The hook destroys its recorder on unmount. The core `HotkeyRecorder` owns the recording listeners. Store the accepted binding in application state rather than relying on recorder session state as your preferences store.\n"}
